# Claude Code's own directory is local — settings.local.json, caches, anything
# a session happens to leave here. But `.claude/rules/` is **project memory**:
# it is most of what used to be CLAUDE.md, split out so it loads per area
# instead of on every turn. Ignored, it existed only in one container — every
# other clone and every cloud session would have read the 219-line root and
# none of the other 123 sections, with nothing anywhere saying so.
# `scripts/memory-is-all-there.mjs` run against a fresh clone is what caught it.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/settings.json
